      "sourceTextSha256": "fe1363e8ddb192a2dbdc2b7d439dc2a08d5f5974bec1a26306387317b5b37a1d",
      "text": "Day 6 · After breakfast, a panoramic city tour (8 hours) introducing Rio’s main attractions in one day. Drive through downtown, with its skyscrapers and colonial architecture, including the Candelária Church, then to the foot of Corcovado, where a small train climbs through the rainforest. A short walk from the last station brings you to the giant statue of Christ the Redeemer, at 710 metres above sea level, with breathtaking views of the city, the Botanical Garden, Maracanã Stadium and Sugar Loaf. Lunch in a typical Brazilian restaurant, then from Praia Vermelha a cable car takes you to Urca Hill and on to Sugar Loaf Mountain, for an unforgettable view of Rio. Return to the hotel with your guide.",
